1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,467
Geppetto, the Puppet Master: he runs his show for a few days, then adds as many

2
00:00:04,467 --> 00:00:06,103
people to his family as he can.

3
00:00:06,323 --> 00:00:07,603
Here's how he plays.

4
00:00:08,433 --> 00:00:12,565
Put the Puppets card next to his Killer board, with all three Puppet tokens on its

5
00:00:12,565 --> 00:00:13,169
Ready space.

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,113
Geppetto's three Puppets are Minions, so the core Minion rules apply, plus a few of

7
00:00:18,113 --> 00:00:18,608
their own.

8
00:00:18,828 --> 00:00:21,336
Each Puppet has one health and an attack of one.

9
00:00:21,336 --> 00:00:25,569
Their Movement Value matches Geppetto's, so they speed up as his Bloodlust rises.

10
00:00:25,789 --> 00:00:29,258
There are only ever three, on the board and the Puppets card combined.

11
00:00:29,258 --> 00:00:32,083
When one is killed, put it on the card's Exhausted space.

12
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:37,161
Until the Finale is revealed, the first step of every Killer phase is to spawn a

13
00:00:37,161 --> 00:00:40,943
Puppet. Take one from the Ready space and place it in Geppetto's space.

14
00:00:41,163 --> 00:00:43,339
If there's none on Ready, nothing spawns.

15
00:00:43,559 --> 00:00:47,339
Either way, then move every Puppet on the Exhausted space back to Ready.

16
00:00:47,339 --> 00:00:50,279
So a Puppet you kill comes back two Killer phases later.

17
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:54,570
Some of his Terror cards say an action line is for the Puppets only.

18
00:00:54,570 --> 00:00:57,223
Many don't, and nor do your location's Terror cards.

19
00:00:57,443 --> 00:01:01,590
When a Killer Action doesn't say it's only for Puppets, every Puppet on the board

20
00:01:01,590 --> 00:01:04,918
resolves the full action, one at a time, in the order you choose.

21
00:01:04,918 --> 00:01:06,659
Then Geppetto resolves it as well.

22
00:01:06,879 --> 00:01:10,399
That's why each extra Puppet on the board makes him much more dangerous.

23
00:01:11,233 --> 00:01:15,129
Puppets are on strings. They must end their movement within two spaces of Geppetto,

24
00:01:15,129 --> 00:01:17,335
though they can pass further away while moving.

25
00:01:17,555 --> 00:01:21,715
If a Puppet must stop because going on would end it more than two spaces away, any

26
00:01:21,715 --> 00:01:23,187
movement it has left is lost.

27
00:01:23,407 --> 00:01:27,821
If an effect leaves a Puppet more than two spaces away, the next time it chooses a

28
00:01:27,821 --> 00:01:32,181
target, it targets Geppetto instead, and stops as soon as it's exactly two spaces

29
00:01:32,181 --> 00:01:32,665
from him.

30
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:37,836
Immortal Master: while all three Puppets are on the board, Geppetto can't be killed.

31
00:01:37,836 --> 00:01:40,881
Damage that would remove his Final Health token is ignored.

32
00:01:41,101 --> 00:01:45,191
Join the Family, his Epic Dark Power: if all three Puppets are in your space during

33
00:01:45,191 --> 00:01:49,232
the Killer phase, you lose all your remaining health, though you still reveal your

34
00:01:49,232 --> 00:01:50,168
Final Health token.

35
00:01:50,388 --> 00:01:54,385
And his Remember Them? Finale spawns every remaining Puppet, though from then on

36
00:01:54,385 --> 00:01:56,233
they move one space less than normal.

37
00:01:57,067 --> 00:02:01,372
A few tips. Every Puppet copies his actions, so killing them cuts his damage, and

38
00:02:01,372 --> 00:02:03,445
keeping one dead stops Immortal Master.

39
00:02:03,665 --> 00:02:07,655
Pick one plan early, rescuing or attacking, rather than splitting your effort.

40
00:02:07,875 --> 00:02:10,612
Watch for Puppets gathering round groups of Victims.

41
00:02:10,612 --> 00:02:11,139
Good luck.

